worked_examples.solution:
(a) Widen the base of the lamp, and lower its centre of gravity (for example, by adding mass low down rather than high up).

(b) A heavy base plate adds mass low down, pulling the overall centre of gravity of the lamp downward, which needs a larger tilt before the weight's line of action leaves the base;

a heavy top would instead raise the centre of gravity and make toppling easier.

theory_blocks.body:
Press a thumbtack into a board and it goes in easily; press on the board with the flat of your hand, using the same force, and nothing happens. The force in both cases can be identical;

what differs is the area over which that force is spread. Concentrating a given force onto a small area has a much greater effect on the surface than spreading the same force over a large area.

This effect is called [[blue:**pressure**]]: how concentrated a force is, over the area it acts on. The same force gives a larger pressure over a smaller area, and a smaller pressure over a larger area.

