theory_blocks.body:
Pressure uses the contact **area**, a two-dimensional surface measured in square metres, never a volume, which is a three-dimensional quantity measured in cubic metres;

the two are not interchangeable and a question's data should be checked for which one it actually provides.

The resulting pressure is measured in [[blue:pascals (or equivalently N/m²)]], never in [[red:newtons alone]]: a pressure answer given in newtons has not actually divided by the area at all.
